    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d102">

                <pb facs="0391" n="289" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg289"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Australian Minister for External Affairs</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Evatt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to President
                        Roosevelt </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-05-13">May 13th, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. President</hi>, In relation to the
                    alternative plan for expanding the Royal Australian Air Force—now under your
                    consideration—I have the honour to inform you that, in duty bound, I raised the
                    matter in the course of my discussions yesterday with the Prime Minister.</p>
                <p>In view of the supreme responsibility vested jointly in yourself and the Prime
                    Minister in connection with such matters, I am expecting that in due course the
                    plan will be considered by you both.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d102-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Yours sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>H V <hi rendition="#small-caps">Evatt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d102-f1" n="1" xml:id="d102-f1-content">
                <p>At the meeting of the Pacific War Council on May 20, Churchill announced that he
                    and Roosevelt had reached agreement on the matter of allocating additional
                    aircraft to Australia; see <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg138">p. 138</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
